  body: |
    # Free in-patient treatment in the ESA special-case source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source defines a patient through free in-patient treatment and requires all stated treatment conditions, with separate private-patient exceptions.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 54003–54005 distinguish the ESA(Cont) and ESA(IR) consequences and retain older NHS legislative citations. Admission, an NHS label or treatment alone does not settle the definition or an award change; present legal and territorial applicability is unresolved.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 54003, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f025dd3bf7f031b0cc9e6/dmgch54.pdf#page=7)
    - [DMG 54004, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f025dd3bf7f031b0cc9e6/dmgch54.pdf#page=9)
    - [DMG 54005, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f025dd3bf7f031b0cc9e6/dmgch54.pdf#page=9)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

